Z||000000||JBGehling||12-05-2000||06:41 PM||||Hey, I was wondering what kind of chance the 88 Fiero GT has of beating a stock base (no special or turbo) 93 Stealth? (both auto)<P>Thanks<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||12-05-2000||06:53 PM||||That Stealth weighs in at around 3400lbs with 160hp(I think that's right..)  They're poochy as hell.  My slightly-better-than-stock GT(now 1FST2M6's) with an automatic could pull on a 3000GT w/auto(naturally aspirated.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||JBGehling||12-05-2000||07:58 PM||||.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>poochy? Sorry, but poochy=good or bad? lol<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-05-2000||08:05 PM||||I destroyed one with my Civic. Go for it!||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||12-05-2000||08:10 PM||||I translate poochy as slightly over weight. I could have misunderstood though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||12-05-2000||08:49 PM||||I thought they were closer to the 220 HP mark, anyways, Bastard is right, their pretty hefty cars. I raced one my friends 91 Non-T and just managed to squeak by him. I have a feeling he would have cleaned me on top end though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JBGehling||12-05-2000||09:01 PM||||I believe the top of the line Stealth is 220, but I'm talking about the base model. <BR>BTW, does anyone know the usual HP of a turbocharged Fiero?<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000007||MachineHead||12-05-2000||09:13 PM||||Turbo Fieros can be in the 200 range.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Got2manyfieros||12-05-2000||09:35 PM||||the base 3000gt is 162 horse I believe, the 3000gt mid model is 220 horse, and the turbo is 300-320 horse depending on the year.   Sorry if that was unclear the first time...<p>[This message has been edited by Got2manyfieros (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||JBGehling||12-05-2000||09:39 PM||||200 HP in a Fiero... yeh!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||12-06-2000||02:23 PM||||I raced Both a Base stealth (destroyed it) the mid range one (no idea on power but it was fadter than the other) beat it by about 4 car lengths , Then I raced a Twin turbo , to about 40mph it was even , Then his turbo's came on and I was done like dinner. I found this to be the same with my friends 300ZX TT , circa 1993 , to 40mph it was a dead heat , then his turbo's spooled up and he was gone. BOth the 300 and the stealth/ 3000GT suffer from massive weight , My friend weighed his 300 in at 3650LBs ..PIG!!! Fiero has great low end torque and weight transfer.. But lacks the top end of the rice rockets.....<P>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000011||loafer87gt||12-06-2000||04:24 PM||||Yep, check it out, it is 222 for non-turbo Stealth/3000GT. 3219 lbs bare bones, 3376 lbs for the loaded model. The turbo models are 300 HP and weight 3800(!!!)pounds. The non turbos do the 1/4 in 15.6, and 0-60 in 7.1 seconds. Basically the same stats as the Nissan 300ZX non-turbos. With a good driver, a 5 speed Stealth/3000GT should be able to keep up or even beat a Fiero GT.<P> <A HREF="http://www.gate.net/~dhaupert/3000faq.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gate.net/~dhaupert/3000faq.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||JBGehling||12-07-2000||09:33 PM||||No need to worry about my next-door neighbor with the stealth... I looked out the window this morning and it was being carried away by a wrecker, lol.<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000013||count_iblis||12-08-2000||09:49 AM||||base stealth =160 hp<BR>ES model=220<BR>Twin turbo=300-320<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
